-- | Whether a diagnostic stops the build — doc 03 §12.7, plan 38.
-- |
-- | Every Redox diagnostic was an error until `RDX1001`. A lint is a
-- | **warning**: it is reported, the build succeeds, and the author decides.
-- | Doc 03 §12.7 — *"`unwrap` and `expect` are lintable rather than
-- | prohibited"*.
-- |
-- | # Why this is not plan 07's level
-- |
-- | `remap.rs` carries rustc's own level as the code's text when rustc gave no
-- | code, which is a different mechanism for a different job: a foreign level
-- | is a string Redox must not interpret, and this is a closed enum that
-- | decides an exit status. Merging them would let rustc's output change
-- | Redox's exit code by spelling, which plan 38 §9's decision 2 rejects.
export data Severity
  -- | Reported, and the build fails. Every diagnostic before `RDX1001`.
  -- |
  -- | The **default**, so no existing construction changes and a new one that
  -- | forgets to say is fatal rather than silent — which is the safe direction
  -- | for the mistake to fall.
  #[default]
  = Error
  -- | Reported, and the build succeeds.
  | Warning
  deriving (Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Default)

instance Severity
  -- | Whether a diagnostic of this severity should stop the build.
  export is_fatal : self -> bool
  is_fatal self = case self of
    Severity::Error -> true
    _ -> false

  -- | `miette`'s equivalent, which is what decides whether the rendered line
  -- | reads `error[RDX…]` or `warning[RDX…]`.
  export to_miette : self -> miette::Severity
  to_miette self = case self of
    Severity::Error -> miette::Severity::Error
    Severity::Warning -> miette::Severity::Warning
